# Private functions
  -- Own stack -- the harness `mk` shape, wired to the real shared facade
  @fn acceptInput()  @ 58-61
      -- Note entry and command dispatch both self-suppress while a toolbar widget holds focus, mirroring
      -- the main grid (trackerRender: inputAllowed folds focusState.acceptCmds). item==nil means dormant.
  -- Editing surface -- bind the pattern-editing subset of the tracker keymap
  @fn setLaneCommands(on)  @ 103-106
      -- Lane editing is poly-only: bind the two commands' keys (Ctrl+Right/Ctrl+Left) while a poly note
      -- editor is open, clear them otherwise, so a mono editor's arrows never add or drop a lane.
  -- Materialise the stored body onto the bound checkout take
  @fn materialiseNotes(specs)  @ 114-123
      -- Specs are park-shaped (logical-only). Route through the authoring add -- the same
      -- tm:addEvent tv's edit.add reaches -- so materialised notes are editable exactly like
      -- typed ones: addEvent takes logical ppq, stamps ppqL/endppqL, files a uuid. rpb rides
      -- like an authored note (tv stamps currentRpb); flush commits. see design/fx-patterns.md § Editing surface
  @fn curveDisplay(body)  @ 131-136
      -- columnDisplay flags for the curve column, from the body's domain + display hint:
      -- normalized -> pb thousandths (bipolar unless 'unipolar'); cc -> 14-bit unless 'cc7'.
  @fn materialiseCurve(body)  @ 138-149
  -- Write-through commit -- persist checkout edits back to the shared store
  @fn readbackBody()  @ 157-201
      -- Read channel 1 back through tm and rebuild the whitelisted body: notes drop fx/chan and fix
      -- lane 1, a curve normalises the pb column's cents to bipolar. lengthPpq/root ride the open
      -- snapshot (no bound command edits them); rpb reads live, so a toolbar change persists with the
      -- body rather than dying with the checkout take. The field pick IS the whitelist. see design/fx-patterns.md § checkout model
  @fn writeThrough()  @ 205-212
      -- Fires on every mini rebuild; `armed` gates out the open/close rebuilds (bindTake, the
      -- materialise flush, the unbind) whose take is not yet/no longer the edited body.
  @fn cancel(close)  @ 217-221
      -- Esc discards: write-through already made the param track the edits, so restore the open
      -- snapshot with one guarded write. Enter needs no counterpart -- the param is already current.
  -- Library copy shelf -- named bodies on the host ds; Save/Load only
  @fn shelf()  @ 309
      -- The shelf lives on the HOST ds (project scope): the mini stack never writes a project tier, and a
      -- shelf edit re-realises nothing (a copy shelf, not live sharing). see docs/patternEditor.md § The copy shelf
  @fn saveShelf(name)  @ 311-315
  @fn deleteShelf(name)  @ 317-321
  @fn maxLane(body)  @ 323-327
  @fn shelfMatches(body)  @ 331-336
      -- Load offers only bodies this editor can materialise: matching kind, curve domain, and (mono) single-lane.
      -- See design/fx-patterns.md § P4 -- polish for the poly-Load gate rationale.
  @fn loadShelf(name)  @ 340-349
      -- Rematerialise a shelf body in place: reopen the checkout on it, keep the modal-open snapshot as
      -- the cancel target, then push the loaded body at the param by hand. see docs/patternEditor.md § The copy shelf
  @fn shelfItems()  @ 352-361
      -- Sorted matching-kind shelf names as picker items; shared by Save and Load.
  @fn drawSave()  @ 365-369
      -- Save and Load are both drawPickers over the matching-kind shelf names; no confirm needed since an
      -- explicit pick/typed-name is itself the confirmation. see docs/patternEditor.md § The copy shelf
  @fn drawLoad()  @ 373-377
      -- Only Load manages the shelf: its rows carry the two-press delete, Save's stay plain.
      -- see docs/patternEditor.md § The copy shelf
  -- Modal editing surface
  @fn drawToolbar()  @ 392-408
      -- Mini toolbar: a copy of the tracker RPB ticker plus Commit/Cancel.
      -- see docs/patternEditor.md § Write-through commit for the button/pendingAction handoff.

# Public API (pe:*)
  @api pe:open(body, commit, poly)  @ 228-287
      @contract  mint a checkout take on scratch, materialise `body`, bind the mini tm; `commit(newBody)` is the write-back  @ 225
      @contract  snapshots the body and arms write-through once materialised (open/close rebuilds stay silent)  @ 226
      @contract  an empty body (no lengthPpq) defaults its loop to one bar of the checkout take  @ 227
  @api pe:close()  @ 291-300
      @contract  sweep the pool metadata (write-through, so leaks without this)  @ 289
      @contract  unbind the mini tm, delete the checkout item  @ 290
  @api pe:isOpen()  @ 302
  @api pe:currentTake()  @ 303
  @api pe:draw()  @ 411-452
      @contract  draw pass -- toolbar row, grid fills the region below; popup sizes to fit  @ 410
  @api pe:handleInput(close)  @ 456-482
      @contract  input pass -- mouse, dispatch against mini cmgr, note entry; unconsumed Esc cancels, Enter commits  @ 454
      @contract  returns the dispatch result kr = { consumed, commandHeld }  @ 455
  @api pe:launch(body, commit, poly)  @ 490-516
      @contract  production entry -- mint the checkout on `body` and raise the editing modal; onClose sweeps it  @ 489

